  "family": "Rhamnaceae",
  "memo": "Coffeeberry is a small tree or large shrub native to oak woodlands, chaparral, coastal scrub, rocky outcrops, and mixed evergreen forests from Oregon to northeastern Mexico. Its reddish stems bear dark green leaves with finely-toothed margins, which curl inward during summer to reduce water loss. Its red drupes appear like small berries, attracting birds and mammals. Each fruit contains two seeds that resemble coffee beans, inspiring its common name. This species is widely cultivated as an ornamental, especially in native gardens, due to its drought tolerance and easy maintenance. It is affected by Sudden Oak Death, which manifests as leaf spots and twig dieback.",
