  "ethnobotanical_info": "This species has vast cultural significance to Native Tribes, who traditionally use the bark as a laxative to treat constipation and the leaves to treat poison oak rashes. The bark contains anthraquinone compounds, which are responsible for its purgative properties and can produce strong side-effects if misused or taken in excess.",
